   "value": "**Result (exact at the numeric point; coefficients fitted at this one point, h = 1/2, θ₁₂ = 31/35).**\n\n**Site 1, all at θ₁−3h.**\n- **What localizes:** **T₍₁,₁₎, T₍₂,₁₎ and T₍₃,₁₎**. This is Paul's guess; for [3,1,0] it was T₍₁,₁₎, T₍₂,₂₎ and T₍₃,₂₎.\n- **Factorization:** ⟨Ω|T_λ(θ₁−3h) = f_λ·⟨Ω_zw|T^{L=1,θ₁}_λ ⊗ ⟨Ω_zw|, with\n  - f₍₁,₁₎ = (θ₁₂−h)(θ₁₂−4h);\n  - f₍₂,₁₎ = (θ₁₂−h)(θ₁₂−2h)(θ₁₂−4h);\n  - f₍₃,₁₎ = (θ₁₂−h)²(θ₁₂−2h)(θ₁₂−4h).\n- **Products:** T₍₁,₁₎·t₁(θ₁−2h) has f = (θ₁₂−h)(θ₁₂−2h)(θ₁₂−4h) and g = f₍₁,₁₎·q₁(θ₁−h), with q₁ = 6h³χ₃ the one-site qdet. It and T₍₃,₁₎·t₂(θ₁+h) add no span.\n- **Span:** rank 4.\n\n**Site 2.**\n- **What localizes:** t₂(θ₂+h) with f = (θ₁₂−2h)(θ₁₂−4h), and the new **T₍₂,₂₎(θ₂)** with f = (θ₁₂−h)(θ₁₂−2h)(θ₁₂−3h)(θ₁₂−4h).\n- **One product:** T₍₂,₂₎(θ₂)·t₁(θ₂−2h) is local, but its site vector is not of the form f·w + g·Ω.\n- **What does not localize:** **t₂(θ₂+h)t₁(θ₂−h)**. It was local for [2,1,0] and [3,1,0].\n- **Span:** rank 4.\n\n**Duality with [3,1,0].** The f's swap sites.\n- [3,2,0] site 2 matches [3,1,0] site 1: T₍₁,₁₎ and T₍₂,₂₎ have the same f's.\n- [3,2,0] site 1 matches [3,1,0] site 2: t₂ with (θ₁₂−h)(θ₁₂−4h), and the product with the same f, g up to sign.\n- This fits [3,2,0] ≅ [3,1,0]* ⊗ det³.\n\n**Reconstruction.** [3,2,0]² = [6,4,0] ⊕ [6,3,1] ⊕ [6,2,2] ⊕ [5,5,0] ⊕ 2[5,4,1] ⊕ 2[5,3,2] ⊕ [4,4,2] ⊕ [4,3,3], i.e. 10 HW states.\n- **Locality at the new twists:** exact at ε = 1/3 for 20 values of w.\n- **site1 + site2 + x₀:** 9 of 10 exact (≤ 4×10⁻⁸⁸). The exception is the bottom irrep **[4,3,3]**: its weight space reaches rank 16 of 18, and the error is ≈ 1.\n- **Adding ⟨Ω(w)|Ψ⟩:** **all 10 exact** (worst 1.7×10⁻⁴⁸ at ε = 10⁻⁹, 4.7×10⁻¹⁰² at 10⁻⁶).\n- **Comparison:** this is the same pattern as [3,1,0], where the missing state was [3,3,2].",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## 6. How many orders of the ε-expansion are needed?\nSection 5 reconstructs Ψ_B at a fixed small ε, i.e. from the *full* finite-ε data. In practice the Q side gives the data as series in ε. Here we ask how many orders are needed to fix the leading term of Ψ_B, which is the CG state.\n\n**Setup.**\n- **Data.** The data matrix M(ε) has rows site1, site2 and Ω for 8 values of w, plus x₀. It is analytic in ε, so M(ε) = Σ_j M_j ε^j.\n- **State.** Ψ_B(ε) = ε^{−k} Σ_j ψ_j ε^j, with ⟨x₀|Ψ⟩ = 1.\n- **Data through order N.** Knowing the data b(ε) = MΨ through relative order N means knowing\n  Σ_{j≤n} M_j ψ_{n−j} = b_n for n = 0..N.\n  This is a block-Toeplitz system in (ψ₀, …, ψ_N).\n\n**Criterion.** ψ₀ is determined iff no null vector of this system has a nonzero ψ₀ part. It is tested in two versions:\n- **(a) with the prior** ψ₀ ∈ HW_μ, since the ε → 0 limit is a highest-weight state (adjoint 11h). Only the HW coordinates of ψ₀ are then unknown.\n- **(b) without it**, so ψ₀ is free in the weight space.\n\n**Numerics.**\n- **Coefficients.** The M_j come from a Cauchy contour, |ε| = 1/8 with 40 points, at 80 digits. Aliasing is about (r/R)^40 ≈ 10⁻²⁰, since the radius of convergence is R ≈ 0.4.\n- **Ranks.** SVDs are done at 30 digits with relative tolerance 10⁻¹². The cell also reports the singular-value gap at that cut.\n- **Divergence.** The leading power k of each HW-limit state is read off from ‖Ψ‖ at ε = 10⁻⁶ and 10⁻⁹.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* stable x0 = e1^T P^-1 with P = L.D.U: P^-1 = U^-1.D^-1.L^-1, no numerical inversion (x0P's Inverse loses all precision at complex ε) *)\nx0S[eps_, pr_] := Module[{zE = N[Exp[eps φT], pr], rsE, Ui, Di, Li}, rsE = rsSol /. Thread[zs -> zE];\n   Ui = nexpS[-((zE[[1]] + zE[[2]])/(zE[[1]] zE[[2]])) EHp[pr][2, 3]] . nexpS[(1/(zE[[1]] zE[[2]])) EHp[pr][1, 3]] . nexpS[-(1/zE[[1]]) EHp[pr][1, 2]];\n   Di = DiagonalMatrix[Table[Product[(s[k] /. rsE)^(-J0[k][p]), {k, 3}], {p, ps[{Λ0}]}]];\n   Li = nexpS[-(r[3] /. rsE) EHp[pr][2, 1]] . nexpS[-(r[2] /. rsE) EHp[pr][3, 1]] . nexpS[-(r[1] /. rsE) EHp[pr][3, 2]];\n   Flatten[KroneckerProduct[#, #]] &[UnitVector[d1, 1] . Ui . Di . Li]];\nchecks[\"stable x0S = x0P (ε = 1/10)\"] = relErr[x0S[1/10, 60], Quiet[x0P[1/10, 60]]];\n(* ‖x0‖ ~ ε^4 here: the row ε^-4 x0 is regular at ε = 0 (rescaling a row by a known function of ε is allowed, <x0|Ψ> = 1 is known exactly) *)\nx0pow = Round[(Log10[Norm[x0S[10^-6, 60]]] - Log10[Norm[x0S[10^-3, 60]]])/(-3)];\n(* Taylor coefficients M_j of the data matrix (site1+site2+Ω rows for 8 w, plus ε^-x0pow x0) from a Cauchy contour in complex ε *)\nfamAll = {\"site1\", \"site2\", \"Ω\"}; ωC = ωMany[[1 ;; 8]];\ndataMat[eps_, ωs_, pr_] := Module[{cf = covFamP[eps, ωs, pr]}, Append[Flatten[Table[Flatten[c /@ famAll, 1], {c, cf}], 1], eps^-x0pow x0S[eps, pr]]];\nrC = 1/8; nP = 40; nMax = 8;\nctr = Table[N[rC Exp[2 Pi I m/nP], 60], {m, 0, nP - 1}];\n{tCtr, matsC} = AbsoluteTiming[dataMat[#, ωC, 60] & /@ ctr];\nMj = Table[N[Sum[matsC[[m]] ctr[[m]]^(-j), {m, nP}]/nP, 30], {j, 0, nMax}];\nepsT = 1/40; resErr = Norm[Flatten[Sum[Mj[[j + 1]] epsT^j, {j, 0, nMax}] - N[dataMat[N[epsT, 60], ωC, 60], 30]]]/Norm[Flatten[Mj[[1]]]];\n(* block-Toeplitz system for orders n = 0..Nn; block 0 is ψ0 = H^T.c (prior) or ψ0 itself *)\ntoep[sec_, Nn_, H_] := Module[{d = Length[sec], m0 = If[H === None, Length[sec], Length[H]], blk},\n   blk[j_] := Mj[[j + 1]][[All, sec]];\n   ArrayFlatten[Table[Table[Which[i > n, ConstantArray[0, {Length[Mj[[1]]], If[i == 0, m0, d]}], i == 0, If[H === None, blk[n], blk[n] . Transpose[H]], True, blk[n - i]], {i, 0, Nn}], {n, 0, Nn}]]];\n(* {norm of the ψ0-part of the null space (0 => ψ0 fixed), log10 singular-value gap at the cut}; threshold relative to the size of the M_j blocks, since M_0 can vanish on a sector *)\npsi0Fixed[sec_, Nn_, H_] := Module[{A = toep[sec, Nn, H], sv, V, m0 = If[H === None, Length[sec], Length[H]], r, scl},\n   scl = Max[Table[Norm[Flatten[Mj[[j + 1]][[All, sec]]]], {j, 0, Nn}]];\n   {sv, V} = {Diagonal[#[[2]]], #[[3]]} &[SingularValueDecomposition[A]];\n   r = Count[sv, x_ /; x > 10^-15 scl];\n   {If[r == Length[V[[1]]], 0, N[Norm[Flatten[V[[1 ;; m0, r + 1 ;;]]]], 3]], If[0 < r < Length[sv], N[Log10[sv[[r + 1]]/sv[[r]]], 3], \"-\"]}];\nnMin[sec_, H_] := Module[{nn = 0, res}, While[nn <= 7 && (res = psi0Fixed[sec, nn, H])[[1]] > 10^-8, nn++]; If[nn > 7, \"> 7\", {nn, res[[2]]}]];\n(* leading divergence k of each HW-limit state, ‖Ψ‖ ~ ε^-k with <x0|Ψ> = 1 *)\nkOf = Module[{a = psiStatesP[10^-6, 200], b = psiStatesP[10^-9, 200]}, Table[{a[[i, \"mu\"]], Round[Log[Norm[b[[i, \"ψ\"]]]/Norm[a[[i, \"ψ\"]]]]/Log[10^3], 1/10]}, {i, Length[a]}]];\n{tTo, depthTab} = AbsoluteTiming[Table[With[{sec = Flatten[Position[wtB, μ]]}, With[{H = N[hwB[μ][[All, sec]], 30]}, {μ, Length[H], Length[sec], Union[Select[kOf, #[[1]] == μ &][[All, 2]]], nMin[sec, H], nMin[sec, None]}]], {μ, hwSecs}]];\nGrid[Join[{{\"contour time (s)\", tCtr, \"resum check at ε=1/40\", ScientificForm[N[resErr, 3], 3], \"x0 ~ ε^\" <> ToString[x0pow], \"\"}, {\"μ\", \"mult\", \"dim\", \"k (Ψ ~ ε^-k)\", \"{N_min, log10 gap}: ψ0 ∈ HW_μ prior\", \"{N_min, log10 gap}: no prior\"}}, depthTab, {{\"time (s)\", tTo}}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"758597\" data-output-id=\"317\" data-out-n=\"310\" data-sub-idx=\"21\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"15\" data-sub-start=\"31\" data-sub-end=\"31\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[310]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:13.24em;vertical-align:-6.35em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:6.89em;\"><span style=\"top:-8.85em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:8.85em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:13.2em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-6.35em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:6.85em;\"><span style=\"top:-9.01em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">contour time (s)</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-7.81em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord mathnormal\">μ</span></span></span><span style=\"top:-6.61em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"minner\"><span class=\"mopen delimcenter\" style=\"top:0em;\">{</span><span class=\"mord\">4</span><span class=\"mpunct\">,</span><span class=\"mspace\" style=\"margin-righ