       "mime": "x-application/wolfram-language-html"
      },
      {
       "data": "Out[294]= \\begin{array}{|c|c|c|c|}\\hline\\varphi  & \\text{s} & \\text{[5,4,1]: c2/c1 of both states} & \\text{[5,3,2]: c2/c1 of both states}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{\\frac{1}{3},-\\frac{2}{7},\\frac{5}{11}\\right\\} & -\\frac{143}{171} & \\left\\{-0.17696717,5.6507657\\right\\} & \\left\\{-0.086071313,11.618273\\right\\}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{\\frac{5}{3},\\frac{3}{7},\\frac{21}{11}\\right\\} & -\\frac{143}{171} & \\left\\{-0.17696717,5.6507657\\right\\} & \\left\\{-0.086071313,11.618273\\right\\}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{\\frac{1}{3},\\frac{1}{5},-\\frac{3}{4}\\right\\} & \\frac{8}{57} & \\left\\{-0.17696717,5.6507657\\right\\} & \\left\\{-0.086071313,11.618273\\right\\}\\\\\\hline\\left\\{0,1,3\\right\\} & \\frac{1}{2} & \\left\\{-0.17696717,5.6507657\\right\\} & \\left\\{-0.086071313,11.618273\\right\\}\\\\\\hline\\text{untwisted eigenbasis} & \\text{z = 1} & \\left\\{-0.17696717,5.6507657\\right\\} & \\left\\{-0.086071313,11.618273\\right\\}\\\\\\hline\\text{HW\\_$\\mu$ invariance residual} &  & 0 & 0\\\\\\hline\\end{array}",
       "mime": "text/plain"
      }
     ],
     "id": "03f3d5d3-1638-4928-9d0d-95eea002d20e"
    }
   ],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "**Result (Section 7).**\n- **No φ-dependence.** The ε → 0 limit vectors in both multiplicity-2 sectors are the same for all four φ (s = −143/171, 8/57, 1/2), to 10⁻⁹ = O(ε).\n- **They are the untwisted eigenbasis.** They coincide, to O(ε), with the eigenvectors of the untwisted inhomogeneous transfer matrices restricted to HW_μ. The two copies are split by θ₁ ≠ θ₂ already at zero twist, so the twist plays no role in choosing the basis.\n- **So the CG basis is canonical:** it is the untwisted inhomogeneous chain's eigenbasis, independent of φ and ω.\n- **Consequences for varying φ:**\n  - It is a consistency check.\n  - It does not supply new target data.\n  - It cannot replace missing data either. Each φ fixes ψ₀ only up to the same kind of ambiguity, and the per-φ normalizations are unrelated, so pooling over φ does not constrain the direction more than one φ does. *(This is an argument, not tested.)*",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 1,
   "value": "## Summary of checks\nBoolean checks must be `True`. Numeric residuals must be below 10⁻²⁵, except the machine-precision ones from Section 1, which must be below 10⁻¹¹.",
   "languageId": "markdown",
   "outputs": [],
   "metadata": {}
  },
  {
   "kind": 2,
   "value": "(* tolerance classes: booleans; \"not a zero test\" sizes; machine-precision residuals; O(ε) residuals from ε = 1e-9 limits; everything else exact-ish (< 1e-25) *)\npassQ[k_, v_] := Which[v === True, True, v === False, False, StringContainsQ[k, \"not a zero test\"], v > 10^-3, StringContainsQ[k, \"O(ε) expected\"], v < 10^-6, StringContainsQ[k, \"machine\"], v < 10^-11, NumericQ[v], v < 10^-25, True, False];\nGrid[Prepend[KeyValueMap[{#1, If[NumericQ[#2], ScientificForm[N[#2, 3], 3], #2], If[passQ[#1, #2], Style[\"PASS\", Darker[Green]], Style[\"FAIL\", Red]]} &, checks], {\"check\", \"value\", \"\"}], Frame -> All, Alignment -> Left]",
   "languageId": "wolfram",
   "outputs": [
    {
     "items": [
      {
       "data": "<div class=\"wl-output-block\"><div class=\"wl-output-header\" style=\"display:flex;align-items:center;gap:6px;width:100%;min-height:22px;\" data-session-epoch=\"758597\" data-output-id=\"318\" data-out-n=\"312\" data-sub-idx=\"2\" data-output-format=\"WLLatex\" data-output-is-graphics=\"0\" data-cell-idx=\"21\" data-sub-start=\"2\" data-sub-end=\"2\"><span style=\"font-size:10px;color:#888;margin-right:8px;\">Out[312]=</span></div><div class=\"wl-output-content\"><div class=\"vscode-wolfram-wllatex-prerendered\" data-page-width-em=\"21\" data-latex-b64=\"\"><span class=\"katex-display\"><span class=\"katex\"><span class=\"katex-html\" aria-hidden=\"true\"><span class=\"base\"><span class=\"strut\" style=\"height:24.04em;vertical-align:-11.75em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:12.29em;\"><span style=\"top:-14.25em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:14.25em;\"></span><span class=\"mtable\"><span class=\"vertical-separator\" style=\"height:24em;border-right-width:0.04em;border-right-style:solid;margin:0 -0.02em;vertical-align:-11.75em;\"></span><span class=\"arraycolsep\" style=\"width:0.5em;\"></span><span class=\"col-align-c\"><span class=\"vlist-t vlist-t2\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:12.25em;\"><span style=\"top:-14.41em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">check</span></span></span></span><span style=\"top:-13.21em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"><span class=\"mord text\"><span class=\"mord\">EH</span><span class=\"mord accent\"><span class=\"vlist-t\"><span class=\"vlist-r\"><span class=\"vlist\" style=\"height:0.6944em;\"><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\"height:3em;\"></span><span class=\"mord\"></span></span><span style=\"top:-3em;\"><span class=\"pstrut\" style=\